{\plain For our immediate purpose, which
 is to find out when J{\fs16 \dn6 n}({\f1 
b}) becomes small with increasing n, for
 fixed {\f1 b}, a {contour plot is helpful
 in observing }{\b Carson's Rule}{:\par 
\par                 that J}{\fs16 \dn6 
n}{(}{\f1 b}{) is approximately 0 when n>}{\f1 
b}{+1.}}
}
.EQN 14 17 16129 0
({0:JJ}NAME)[({0:n}NAME,{0:\b}NAME):{0:Jn}NAME({0:n}NAME,{0:\b}NAME)
.EQN 7 -9 16130 0
{0:JJ}NAME{0 1 1 4 0 35 36 1 1 4 1 1 1 1 1 14 0 8 0 8 3 Carson's^Rule}{57}
